Q.9 \textbf{Kathak is a classical dance form that developed in which
region of India?}

A. Southern India\\
B. Northern India\\
C. Eastern India\\
D. Western India

Answer: B

Sol: The correct answer is: (b) Northern India.

Explanation:\\
• Kathak is a classical dance form that originated in Northern India,
particularly in the regions of Uttar Pradesh, Rajasthan, and Madhya
Pradesh.• Kathak, which means "storytelling" in Sanskrit, is known for
its intricate footwork, spins, and expressive movements.

• It was originally a form of temple dance and later evolved to be
performed in the royal courts, especially under the patronage of the
Mughal emperors.

Information Booster:\\
• Kathak is one of the eight classical dance forms of India.

• It combines narrative storytelling with rhythmic footwork and
expressive gestures, making it unique among Indian classical dances.

