Q.10 \textbf{Which of the following is not a Maharatna company as of
2024?}

A. Hindustan Copper Limited\\
B. National Thermal Power Corporation Limited\\
C. Oil \& Natural Gas Corporation Limited\\
D. Steel Authority of India Limited

Answer: A

Sol: The correct answer is: (a) Hindustan Copper Limited.

Explanation:\\
• As of 2024, Hindustan Copper Limited (HCL) is not a Maharatna company.

• Maharatna status is a prestigious recognition given to certain public
sector enterprises in India, allowing them greater autonomy in
decision-making.

• The companies in the options that have Maharatna status are:\\
· National Thermal Power Corporation Limited (NTPC)\\
· Oil \& Natural Gas Corporation Limited (ONGC)\\
· Steel Authority of India Limited (SAIL)\\
Information Booster:\\
• The Maharatna status allows a company to make investment decisions up
to ₹5,000 crores without government approval.

• Hindustan Copper Limited has not yet been granted Maharatna status,
though it is a significant player in the mining sector.

Q.11 \textbf{Which Indian state was the first to benefit from the Green
Revolution?}

A. Haryana\\
B. Uttar Pradesh\\
C. Rajasthan\\
D. Punjab

Answer: D

Sol: The correct answer is: (d) Punjab.

Explanation:\\
• Punjab was the first state in India to benefit from the Green
Revolution, which started in 1960s.

• The Green Revolution involved the introduction of high-yielding
variety (HYV) seeds, modern irrigation techniques, and the use of
chemical fertilizers.

• Punjab was the pioneer in adopting these agricultural technologies,
resulting in a significant increase in the production of wheat and rice.

• The state became the breadbasket of India, helping the country achieve
self-sufficiency in food production by the 1970s.

Information Booster:\\
• The Green Revolution was initiated under the leadership of Dr. M.S.
Swaminathan in the 1960s.

• The Green Revolution began in Punjab in 1966 and extended to other
states like Haryana and Uttar Pradesh by the 1970s.

• By the 1980s, India had achieved food self-sufficiency, largely due to
the success of the Green Revolution.

Additional Knowledge:\\
• The Green Revolution is credited with transforming
India\textquotesingle s agricultural sector, but its benefits were not
uniformly distributed, as some areas lagged behind in adopting modern
techniques.• The revolution was largely focused on wheat and rice, while
crops like millets and pulses were neglected.

Q.12 \textbf{Which of the following pairs is correctly matched?}

A. Plasmolysis - Gain of water by plant cell\\
B. Cell wall - Composed mainly of protein\\
C. Cellulose - Provides structural strength to plant cells\\
D. Plasma membrane - Located outside the cell wall

Answer: C

Sol: The correct answer is: (c) Cellulose - Provides structural strength
to plant cells.
\end{quote}

\begin{longtable}[]{@{}
  >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\columnwidth - 0\tabcolsep) * \real{1.0000}}@{}}
\toprule()
