Q.17 \textbf{What was the key scientific objective of Chandrayaan-3?}

A. To demonstrate a safe lunar landing and rover operation\\
B. To study Mars\textquotesingle{} atmosphere\\
C. To measure gravitational waves\\
D. To orbit the Moon

Answer: A

Sol: The correct answer is: (a) To demonstrate a safe lunar landing and
rover operation.

Explanation:\\
• The Chandrayaan-3 mission by ISRO was focused on demonstrating India's
capability to achieve a safe lunar landing and operate a rover on the
Moon's surface.

• It was designed to build upon the success of Chandrayaan-1 and the
lessons learned from the Chandrayaan-2 mission. The
rover\textquotesingle s primary task was to explore the lunar surface
and send valuable data back to Earth.

Information Booster:\\
• Chandrayaan-1 (2008) was India's first lunar mission, which discovered
water molecules on the Moon.

• Chandrayaan-2 (2019) included an orbiter, lander, and rover, but the
lander lost communication during the descent.

• Chandrayaan-3 aimed to successfully land on the Moon and demonstrate
operational capabilities in lunar exploration.

Q.18 \textbf{Who became Indian Navy\textquotesingle s first woman
fighter pilot streamer on 3 July 2025?}

A. Bina Kumar\\
B. Vidya Singh\\
C. Neha Sharma\\
D. Aastha Poonia

Answer: D

Sol: The correct answer is: (d) Aastha Poonia.

Explanation:\\
• Aastha Poonia became the Indian Navy\textquotesingle s first woman
fighter pilot streamer on 3 July 2025, marking a historic achievement in
Indian defense forces.

• This milestone reflects the growing gender inclusivity in
India\textquotesingle s armed forces, particularly in the combat roles
traditionally dominated by men.

Information Booster:\\
• Indian Navy: Aastha Poonia\textquotesingle s achievement is a
significant step for women\textquotesingle s empowerment in the
military, following the Indian Air Force\textquotesingle s earlier
induction of women into combat roles.• Women Fighter Pilots: India has
been gradually integrating more women into combat roles across the armed
forces, with other services following suit.

Q.19 \textbf{Which constitutional amendment is known as the "Mini
Constitution"?}

A. 52nd Amendment\\
B. 44th Amendment\\
C. 42nd Amendment\\
D. 24th Amendment

Answer: C

Sol: The correct answer is: (c) 42nd Amendment.

Explanation:\\
• The 42nd Constitutional Amendment, passed in 1976, is known as the
"Mini Constitution" because it introduced extensive changes to the
Indian Constitution.

• The amendment increased the power of the central government, reduced
the powers of the judiciary, and subordinated the Directive Principles
of State Policy to the Fundamental Rights.

• It also introduced Fundamental Duties for the first time under Article
51A, which outlines the duties of Indian citizens to respect the
Constitution and contribute to national harmony.

Information Booster:\\
• The 42nd Amendment also curtailed the role of the judiciary in matters
related to the enforcement of the Fundamental Rights.

• It introduced the concept of "equality before law" in the
administration of justice and the prevention of political interference
in the legal system.

Additional Knowledge:\\
