\includegraphics[width=2.33889in,height=0.48889in]{vertopal_3d0b0d13ceb344a0aa13e91d868b487a/media/image7.png}
\includegraphics[width=2.33889in,height=0.69028in]{vertopal_3d0b0d13ceb344a0aa13e91d868b487a/media/image11.png}

• The Khajuraho temples are known for their sculptural beauty, with
intricate carvings depicting both religious themes and erotic art,
symbolizing the temple\textquotesingle s celebration of life.• The
Chandela dynasty, which ruled between the 9th and 13th centuries, built
many temples in the Khajuraho region, making it an important cultural
and architectural site in Indian history.

Q.25 \textbf{What are the streams of charged particles ejected by the
Sun into space called?}

A. Sunspots\\
B. Solar wind\\
C. Solar flares\\
D. Coronal loops

Answer: B

Sol: The correct answer is: (b) Solar wind.

Explanation:\\
• The solar wind consists of charged particles, primarily electrons and
protons, that are ejected from the Sun into space.

• These particles travel across the solar system at high speeds and can
have significant effects on space weather and the Earth's magnetic
field, often causing phenomena like the aurora borealis (Northern
Lights).

• Solar wind plays a key role in the interaction between the Sun and the
planets, including the Earth.

Information Booster:\\
• The solar wind is primarily driven by the Sun\textquotesingle s
corona, which is the outermost layer of the Sun\textquotesingle s
atmosphere. The corona's temperature is much higher than that of the
Sun\textquotesingle s surface, allowing particles to escape into space.

• Sunspots (Option a) are dark patches on the Sun\textquotesingle s
surface, caused by magnetic activity, but they are not charged particle
streams.

• Solar flares (Option c) are intense bursts of energy and radiation
from the Sun, not streams of charged particles.

• Coronal loops (Option d) are large, arching loops of solar material,
typically associated with magnetic fields, and are different from the
solar wind.

Additional Knowledge:\\
• The solar wind interacts with Earth\textquotesingle s magnetic field,
causing geomagnetic storms, which can disrupt satellites, GPS systems,
and power grids.

• The speed of the solar wind can vary but typically ranges from 300 to
800 km/s.

Q.26 \textbf{Which of the following statements is NOT TRUE about Rash
Behari Bose?}

A. He founded Indian Independence League in Tokyo in 1942.

B. He was an important figure in the Ghadar Movement and in the
formation of the Azad Hind Fauj.\\
C. He was honoured with the prestigious title \textquotesingle Order of
the rising sun\textquotesingle.

D. He was independent India\textquotesingle s first Commander-in-Chief
of Indian Army.

Answer: D

Sol: The correct answer is: (d) He was independent
India\textquotesingle s first Commander-in-Chief of Indian Army.

Explanation:\\
Independent India\textquotesingle s first Commander-in-Chief of the
Indian Army was Field Marshal K. M. Cariappa, who took on the role after
the country\textquotesingle s independence in 1947.• Rash Behari Bose
was a revolutionary figure in India\textquotesingle s fight for
independence. Mohan Singh was its initial founder and commander. Subhas
Chandra Bose was the Commander-in-Chief of the Indian National Army
(INA) from 1943 until its end.

• Rash Behari Bose played a key role in the Ghadar Movement and the
Indian Independence League but did not hold the position of
Commander-in-Chief in independent India.

Information Booster:\\
• Ghadar Movement: Rash Behari Bose was one of the key figures in the
Ghadar Movement, which aimed at overthrowing British rule by
revolutionary means.

• Indian Independence League: Rash Behari Bose founded the Indian
Independence League in Tokyo in 1942, which later played a role in
organizing the Azad Hind Fauj (INA) under Subhas Chandra Bose.

• Order of the Rising Sun: Rash Behari Bose was conferred with the Order
of the Rising Sun by Japan for his efforts in the Indian independence
movement.

Q.27 \textbf{What is the role of the Foreigners\textquotesingle{}
Tribunal in the NRC (National Register of Citizens) process?}

A. To conduct the Census\\
B. To issue voter ID cards\\
C. To deport illegal immigrants\\
D. To verify citizenship claims of individuals excluded from the NRC

Answer: D

Sol: The correct answer is: (d) To verify citizenship claims of
individuals excluded from the NRC.

Explanation:\\
• The Foreigners\textquotesingle{} Tribunal plays a crucial role in the
NRC process by verifying the citizenship claims of individuals who have
been excluded from the final list of the National Register of Citizens.

• The tribunal assesses whether a person can prove that they are a
citizen of India or not, and it has the authority to determine the
legality of their stay in India.

• If an individual is declared an illegal immigrant, they can be
deported or sent to detention centers.

Information Booster:\\
• The NRC is a register of Indian citizens in the state of Assam, and
the process aims to identify illegal immigrants who have entered India,
particularly from neighboring Bangladesh.• The
Foreigners\textquotesingle{} Tribunal is part of a judicial system where
appeals and claims of citizenship are processed in a fair manner.

Q.28 \textbf{Which countries are members of BIMSTEC?}

A. Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Pakistan, Nepal, Sri Lanka, Thailand\\
B. Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Myanmar, Maldives, Sri Lanka, Thailand\\
C. Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Myanmar, Nepal, Sri Lanka, Thailand\\
D. Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Maldives, Nepal, Pakistan,
Sri Lanka

Answer: C

Sol: The correct answer is: (c) Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Myanmar,
Nepal, Sri Lanka, Thailand.

Explanation:\\
• BIMSTEC (Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and
Economic Cooperation) is a regional organization comprising countries
from South Asia and Southeast Asia.• It includes Bangladesh, Bhutan,
India, Myanmar, Nepal, Sri Lanka, and Thailand. These seven countries
collaborate on various sectors such as trade, technology, and
environmental sustainability.

Information Booster:\\
• Pakistan and Maldives: Neither Pakistan nor Maldives is a member of
BIMSTEC.

• BIMSTEC's Purpose: The main objective of BIMSTEC is to enhance
regional connectivity and cooperation among member countries in multiple
areas like trade, energy, tourism, and agriculture.

Additional Knowledge:\\
• BIMSTEC was established in 1997 and serves as a bridge between South
Asia and Southeast Asia.

