Q.30 \textbf{Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct
regarding the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS)?}\\
\textbf{1. The Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita introduces community service as a
punishment for minor offences.}

\textbf{2. The scope of summary trials has been limited to only serious
offences under the new law.}\\
\textbf{3. The reformative approach aims to ensure societal
reintegration of offenders.}

A. 1 and 2 only\\
B. 1 and 3 only\\
C. 2 and 3 only\\
D. 1, 2, and 3 all are correct

Answer: B

Sol: The correct answer is: (b) 1 and 3 only.

Explanation:\\
• The Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), introduced as part of the criminal
law reform in India, focuses on improving the justice system with a
reformative approach.• Statement 1 is correct: The BNS introduces
community service as an alternative punishment for minor offences,
promoting rehabilitation.

• Statement 2 is incorrect: The scope of summary trials has been
expanded, not limited, to include both minor and serious offences under
the new law.• Statement 3 is correct: The BNS adopts a reformative
approach, focusing on societal reintegration of offenders rather than
just punishment.

Information Booster:\\
• The BNS is a part of India's ongoing efforts to overhaul its criminal
justice system to make it more humane, effective, and efficient.

• The law aims to create a restorative justice system that focuses on
rehabilitation and reintegration of offenders into society.

• The BNS also includes provisions for reducing prison overcrowding by
offering alternatives to incarceration for minor crimes.

Additional Knowledge:\\
• BNS is a part of the broader criminal law reform initiated in India,
addressing the need for modernization and streamlining of processes in
the judicial system.

Q.31 \textbf{Which Indian-American author wrote The Namesake, later
adapted into a film?}

A. Kiran Desai\\
B. Jhumpa Lahiri\\
C. Arundhati Roy\\
D. Chetan Bhagat

Answer: B

Sol: The correct answer is: (b) Jhumpa Lahiri.

Explanation:\\
• Jhumpa Lahiri, an Indian-American author, wrote the novel The
Namesake, which was later adapted into a critically acclaimed film in
2006.\\
• The novel explores themes of identity, immigration, and the challenges
faced by first-generation immigrants in the United States.

Information Booster:\\
• Kiran Desai (Option a) is another acclaimed author known for her novel
The Inheritance of Loss, which won the Booker Prize in 2006.

• Arundhati Roy (Option c) is famous for her novel The God of Small
Things, which won the Booker Prize in 1997.

• Chetan Bhagat (Option d) is a popular Indian author known for novels
like Five Point Someone and 2 States, but he is not the author of The
Namesake.

Q.32 \textbf{What was the role of the University Grants Commission
(UGC), established in 1956?}

A. To regulate trade agreements\\
B. To promote agricultural development\\
C. To manage industrial policies\\
D. To oversee and fund higher education institutions in India

Answer: D

Sol: The correct answer is: (d) To oversee and fund higher education
institutions in India.

Explanation:\\
• The University Grants Commission (UGC) was established in 1956 by an
Act of Parliament with the aim to coordinate, determine, and maintain
the standards of higher education in India.• UGC's key role includes
disbursing funds to universities and colleges, ensuring the quality of
education, and regulating academic policies in the higher education
sector.

• It also ensures that educational institutions comply with certain
academic standards and infrastructure norms.

Information Booster:\\
• The UGC also monitors the accreditation process of universities and
plays a role in regulating courses and curriculum at the undergraduate
and postgraduate levels.

• The UGC is responsible for conducting the National Eligibility Test
(NET) for determining eligibility for university-level teaching jobs.

Q.33 \textbf{Which of the following is a characteristic feature of the
Western Coastal Plains?}

A. Mangrove forests\\
B. High rainfall\\
C. Large deltas\\
D. Lagoons and backwaters

Answer: D

Sol: The correct answer is: (d) Lagoons and backwaters.

Explanation:\\
• The Western Coastal Plains are characterized by features like lagoons
and backwaters, particularly in states like Kerala and Goa.\\
• These coastal plains are formed by the Arabian Sea and are known for
their calm waters and rich biodiversity.

• The backwaters of Kerala are particularly famous for their natural
beauty, tourism, and unique ecosystem.

Information Booster:\\
