Q.34 \textbf{Which level of the Panchayati Raj system operates at the
village level?}

A. Panchayat Samiti\\
B. Zila Parishad\\
C. Gram Panchayat\\
D. Gram Sabha

Answer: C

Sol: The correct answer is: (c) Gram Panchayat.

Explanation:\\
• The Gram Panchayat is the lowest level of the Panchayati Raj system
and operates at the village level. It is responsible for local
governance and community welfare, including education, health, and
infrastructure development.
\end{quote}

• The Gram Panchayat is directly elected by the people of the village
and is empowered to make decisions on issues concerning the village. It
is a self-governing body at the grassroots level.

\begin{quote}
Related Articles, Parts, and Amendments:\\
• Article 243: This article in the Constitution of India mentions the
establishment of Panchayats at various levels: Gram Panchayat (village
level), Panchayat Samiti (block level), and Zila Parishad (district
level).

• Article 243B: Provides for the constitution of Panchayats at the
village, intermediate, and district levels, as per the Constitution
(73rd Amendment) Act, 1992.

Related Amendments:\\
· 73rd Amendment Act (1992): The 73rd Constitutional Amendment provided
for the constitutional recognition of Panchayati Raj Institutions
(PRIs). It mandates that Gram Panchayats, Panchayat Samitis, and Zila
Parishads be established in rural areas for decentralized governance.

· It also ensures direct elections at each level of Panchayats and gives
them the authority to handle local governance functions.

Additional Information:\\
• Gram Sabha (Option d) is a body of all adult members of the village
and serves as the general assembly for decision-making. It discusses and
approves the Gram Panchayat\textquotesingle s activities and decisions.

• The Panchayati Raj system was introduced to promote decentralized
governance, ensure participation of people in local decision-making, and
improve accountability at the grassroots level.

Q.35 \textbf{Consider the following two statements, labeled Assertion
(A) and Reason (R). Evaluate them and choose the appropriate answer from
the given options.} \textbf{Assertion (A): India\textquotesingle s
participation in the Asian Winter Games 2025 will be unique, as it will
be the first time the government has provided full financial support.}

\textbf{Reason (R): The government\textquotesingle s objective is to
enhance India\textquotesingle s presence and performance in winter
sports by ensuring fair and meritocratic athlete selection.}

A. A is true, but R is false.

B. Both A and R are true, but R is not the correct explanation of A.

C. Both A and R are true, and R is the correct explanation of A .

D. Not Answered

Answer: C

Sol: The correct answer is: (c) Both A and R are true, and R is the
correct explanation of A.

Explanation:\\
· Assertion (A) is true: India's participation in the Asian Winter Games
2025 in Harbin, China is historic as, for the first time, the Government
of India will fully fund the Indian contingent's participation. This was
confirmed by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports (MYAS).

· Reason (R) is also true and explains the assertion correctly: The
decision for full funding stems from the government\textquotesingle s
strategic aim to promote winter sports, ensure fair selection based on
merit, and build global competitiveness. The support is part of the
broader vision to diversify India\textquotesingle s sporting profile and
boost excellence.

Information Booster:\\
· Host City: The 10th Asian Winter Games will be held in Harbin, China
from February 7 to 14, 2025.

· First Full Funding: This is the first time ever India's entire winter
sports contingent will be funded by the Government of India, not the
athletes or private federations.

· Previous Participation: India has participated in past Asian Winter
Games but funding was partial or private, limiting athlete inclusion.

· Athletes' Training: Selection will be based on training under the
Target Olympic Podium Scheme (TOPS) and Khelo India framework.

· Disciplines: India is expected to participate in events like alpine
skiing, cross-country skiing, figure skating, and snowboarding.

Additional Knowledge:\\
· Why other options are incorrect:\\
· \emph{(a)} is incorrect because Reason is true.

· \emph{(b)} is incorrect because R clearly explains A, tying policy to
purpose.

· Winter Sports Push: The government has also committed to developing
infrastructure in Ladakh, Himachal, and Jammu \& Kashmir to promote
winter sports.

· Asian Winter Games 2017: Held in Sapporo and Obihiro, Japan, India
sent a smaller, self-funded contingent.

· Global Strategy: India aims to expand representation beyond
traditional sports by investing in niche disciplines like winter sports
and fencing.

· Policy Initiative: This move aligns with India's Sports Policy Vision
2047, which aims at broad-based sports excellence across diverse
climatic regions.

Q.36 \textbf{At what orientation does a rotating coil in a uniform
magnetic field generate the maximum induced EMF?}

A. When the coil\textquotesingle s plane is at 45° to the magnetic field
lines\\
B. When the magnetic flux through the coil is maximum\\
C. When the coil\textquotesingle s plane is perpendicular (90°) to the
magnetic field lines\\
D. When the coil\textquotesingle s plane is parallel to the magnetic
field lines

Answer: D

Sol: The correct answer is: (d) When the coil\textquotesingle s plane is
parallel to the magnetic field lines.

Explanation:\\
• the maximum induced EMF occurs when the plane of the coil is parallel
to the magnetic field lines, not when it\textquotesingle s perpendicular
to them.

• When the plane of the coil is parallel to the magnetic field, the
magnetic flux through the coil is maximum (or zero if using the flux
formula involving sine), but the rate of change of magnetic flux is
zero. This results in zero induced EMF, not the highest EMF. The highest
EMF is induced when the normal to the plane of the coil is parallel to
the magnetic field, causing the magnetic flux to change at its maximum
rate.

Information Booster:\\
• The induced EMF follows Faraday's Law of Induction, which states that
EMF = -dΦ/dt, where Φ is the magnetic flux. The rate of change of flux
is highest when the coil's orientation changes most rapidly with respect
to the magnetic field.

Q.37 \textbf{What does the term "checkmate" refer to in chess?}

A. End of game\\
B. Invalid move\\
C. A draw\\
D. A win

Answer: A

Sol: The correct answer is: (a) End of game.

Explanation:\\
• Checkmate is a term in chess that signifies the end of the game.

• It occurs when a player\textquotesingle s king is placed in check
(under threat of capture), and there is no legal move left to escape the
check.
