Q.38 \textbf{What shape does a population pyramid take for a rapidly
growing population?}

A. Inverted triangle shape\\
B. Circular shape\\
C. Triangular shape\\
D. Rectangular shape

Answer: C

Sol: The correct answer is: (c) Triangular shape.

Explanation:\\
• A triangular shape in a population pyramid indicates a rapidly growing
population.

• This shape is characterized by a wide base (representing a high birth
rate) and a narrow top (representing a smaller elderly population),
which is typical of countries with high birth rates and young
populations.

Information Booster:\\
• Inverted Triangle Shape (a): An inverted triangle usually represents a
declining population, where the elderly population is larger than the
younger generation.

• Circular Shape (b): A circular shape is uncommon in population
pyramids and does not typically represent demographic trends.

• Rectangular Shape (d): A rectangular shape suggests a stable or
slow-growing population, with roughly equal proportions across age
groups.

Q.39 \textbf{Which of the following was a major effect of the 42nd
Constitutional Amendment?}

A. It abolished the Directive Principles of State Policy.

B. It increased the tenure of the Lok Sabha and introduced Fundamental
Duties\\
C. It introduced Fundamental Rights for citizens.

D. It reduced the term of the Lok Sabha to four years

Answer: B

Sol: The correct answer is: (b) It increased the tenure of the Lok Sabha
and introduced Fundamental Duties.

Explanation:\\
• The 42nd Constitutional Amendment, passed in 1976, brought several
significant changes to the Indian Constitution.

• Among its major effects were:\\
· Increase in the tenure of the Lok Sabha from 5 years to 6 years.

· Introduction of Fundamental Duties under Article 51A, which enumerates
the duties of citizens to respect the Constitution and promote harmony
in the country.

Information Booster:\\
• The amendment made the Directive Principles of State Policy
subordinate to Fundamental Rights, meaning the state's obligation to
fulfill these principles could be seen in the light of individual
rights.• The amendment also curtailed the power of the judiciary in
certain matters, marking a significant shift in the balance of power
between the legislature and the judiciary.

Additional Knowledge:\\
• The 42nd Amendment is often referred to as the ``mini-Constitution''
because of the wide range of changes it introduced.

• Another important change was the shift in the balance of power, giving
the central government more authority over state governments,
particularly in matters related to emergency provisions.• This amendment
was later partly reversed by the 44th Amendment (1978), which restored
the Lok Sabha\textquotesingle s term to 5 years and made other key
changes.

Q.40 \textbf{Which Pratihara ruler successfully repelled Arab invasions
in North-Western India?}

A. Mihira Bhoja\\
B. Nagabhata I\\
C. Rajyapala\\
D. Vatsaraja

Answer: B

Sol: The correct answer is: (b) Nagabhata I.

Explanation:\\
• Nagabhata I was a ruler of the Pratihara dynasty who is famous for
successfully repelling the Arab invasions in the north-western part of
India.

• He fought the Arab invaders in the 8th century, particularly during
the Battle of Rajasthan around 730 AD, where he halted the progress of
Arab forces who had previously made inroads into India.

• Nagabhata I's defense ensured the survival of Hindu kingdoms in the
region and prevented the spread of Islamic influence in north-western
India at that time.

Information Booster:\\
• Mihira Bhoja (Option a): Mihira Bhoja was another prominent ruler of
the Pratihara dynasty who succeeded Nagabhata I, and his reign was
marked by military conquests and the expansion of the Pratihara empire.

• Rajyapala (Option c): Rajyapala was a later Pratihara ruler, but he is
not specifically known for repelling the Arab invasions.

• Vatsaraja (Option d): Vatsaraja was also a Pratihara ruler, but he
faced defeat against the combined forces of the Rashtrakutas and the
Arab invaders during his reign.

