Q.50 \textbf{Which of the following statements is/are correct?}

\textbf{Statement I: A bank\textquotesingle s main liability is the
deposits it holds.}

\textbf{Statement II: Open Market Operations involve buying and selling
government bonds.}

\textbf{Statement III: The Bank Rate is the rate at which RBI lends to
commercial banks.}

A. Only Statement III is correct\\
B. I, II and III all three statements are correct\\
C. Only Statements I and II are correct\\
D. Only Statements II and III are correct

Answer: B

Sol: The correct answer is: (b) I, II and III all three statements are
correct.

Explanation:\\
• Statement I: A bank\textquotesingle s main liability is indeed the
deposits it holds, as the money deposited by customers is a liability
for the bank.

• Statement II: Open Market Operations (OMO) refer to the buying and
selling of government securities by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) in
the open market to regulate liquidity in the economy.

• Statement III: The Bank Rate is the rate at which the RBI lends to
commercial banks against approved securities. It is one of the tools of
monetary policy to control inflation and money supply.

Information Booster:\\
• RBI\textquotesingle s Role: The Reserve Bank of India uses various
tools such as repo rates, reverse repo rates, and bank rates to manage
the money supply and influence interest rates in the economy.

