PLAY→ RNCA\\
Thus, correct option is (a).

Q.55 \textbf{In a row of 8 seats, how many ways can 3 people sit next to
each other?}

A. 72\\
B. 36\\
C. 48\\
D. 54

Answer: B

Sol: \hspace{0pt}Think of the 3 people as one block.

This block can sit in 6 places (like seats 1--3, 2--4, \ldots, 6--8).

Inside the block, the 3 people can sit in 3! = 6 ways.

So total = 6 × 6 = 36\\
Thus, correct option is (b).

