Q.58 \textbf{If 3x+y=12 and x-y=4 what is the value of x ?}

A. 2\\
B. 4\\
C. 6\\
D. 8

Answer: B

Sol: Given:\\
3x+y=12 and x-y=4\\
To find: Value of x\\
Solution:\\
Adding both equations:\\
We get,\\
3\emph{x} + \emph{y} + \emph{x} −\emph{y} = 12 + 4\\
4\emph{x} = 16\\
\emph{x} = 4

Hence Option B is the correct answer.
\end{quote}

