Q.60 \textbf{Find the next term in the given letter series: ZZPQPQPQ,
PZZPQPQP , PQZZPQPQ, PQPZZPQP , PQPQZZPQ, \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ .}

A. PQPQPZZP\\
B. PQPQZZPQ\\
C. ZZPQPQPQ\\
D. PZZPQPQP

Answer: A

Sol: The correct answer is option (a).

Logic that follows: The block ``ZZ'' slides one position to the right at
each step (occupying pairs 1--2, then 2--3, then 3--4, and so on).\\
The position where ZZ used to start is filled with letters that
alternate P, Q, P, Q, \ldots{} starting with P.

Applying this to the series:\\
ZZ at 1--2 → ZZPQPQPQ\\
ZZ at 2--3; fill left position with P → PZZPQPQP\\
ZZ at 3--4; fill left position with Q → PQZZPQPQ\\
ZZ at 4--5; fill left position with P → PQPZZPQP\\
ZZ at 5--6; fill left position with Q → PQPQZZPQ\\
ZZ at 6--7; fill left position with P → PQPQPZZP\\
So the next term is PQPQPZZP (Option A).

Hence option a is the correct answer.

