Q.69 \textbf{Find the ODD one out.}

A. Cube\\
B. Sphere\\
C. Cylinder\\
D. Cone

Answer: A

Sol: \hspace{0pt}(A) Cube -- only flat surfaces, no curved surface.

(B) Sphere -- curved surface, no edges or corners.\\
(C) Cylinder -- curved surface + flat circles.

(D) Cone -- curved surface + flat circle + a corner.\\
Odd one: Cube (A), because it has no curved surface.\\
Thus, correct option is (a).

Q.70 \textbf{Which of the following conclusions can be logically drawn
from the statement?}\\
\textbf{"All apples are fruits. Some fruits are sour."}

A. Some fruits may not be apples.\\
B. Some apples are not fruits.\\
C. All sour things are fruits.\\
D. All apples are sour.

Answer: A

Sol: Statement:\\
All apples are fruits.

Some fruits are sour.

(A) Some fruits may not be apples.

Correct, because ``all apples are fruits'' does not mean all fruits are
apples.\\
(B) Some apples are not fruits.

Wrong, because it clearly says all apples are fruits.

(C) All sour things are fruits.

Wrong, we only know some fruits are sour, not that everything sour must
be fruit.\\
(D) All apples are sour.

Wrong, nothing about all apples being sour.

So, Some fruits may not be apples.

Thus, correct option is (a).

