WYAC: W→Y (+2), Y→A (+2, wrap after Z), A→C (+2) Correct\\
ACED: A→C (+2), C→E (+2), E→D (−1) This is incorrect.

Why ACED doesn't belong:

It breaks the consistent ``+2 each step'' pattern at the end (E to D
goes backward), so ACED is the only one not following the rule.

Q.76 \textbf{If Neha is facing south and turns 90}∘ \textbf{to her left,
then 180}∘ \textbf{to her right, and finally 90}∘ \textbf{to her left
again, which direction is she facing now?}

A. West\\
B. North\\
C. South\\
D. East

Answer: C

Sol: Given:\\
Neha faces South → turns 90° left, then 180° right, then 90° left.\\
Now, we check step-by-step.

South ---(90° left)→ East ---(180° right)→ West ---(90° left)→ South.

So, the following direction is: South.\\
Thus, correct option is (c).
\end{quote}

