Q.80 \textbf{The sum of the ages of A and B is 46 years. Five years ago,
the ratio of their ages was 4 : 5. What is B's current age?}

A. 21 Years\\
B. 20 years\\
C. 24 years\\
D. 25 years

Answer: D

Sol: Given:\\
Sum of the ages of A and B = 46\\
Ratio of their ages 5 years ago = 4 : 5\\
Solution:\\
Five years ago,\\
Let the age of A = 4x\\
and age of B = 5x\\
Present Sum of the ages A and B\\
4\emph{x} + 5 + 5\emph{x} + 5 = 46\\
9\emph{x} = 36\\
\emph{x} = 4\\
\hspace{0pt}\\
Present age of B = 5\emph{x} + 5 = 5 × 4 + 5 = 25\\
Hence option D is the correct answer.
\end{quote}

