Q.85 \textbf{Read the following statement carefully and identify the
conclusion that follows.}\\
\textbf{Statements: All flowers are trees. Some trees are plants.}

\textbf{Conclusions:}\\
\textbf{I. Some flowers are plants.}

\textbf{II. All flowers are plants.}

A. Neither I nor II follows\\
B. Both I and II follow\\
C. Only Conclusion I follows\\
D. Only Conclusion II follows

Answer: A

Sol: Statements:\\
All flowers are trees.

Some trees are plants.

From the given statements Venn diagram will be:

\includegraphics[width=1.76389in,height=0.81944in]{vertopal_3d0b0d13ceb344a0aa13e91d868b487a/media/image27.png}

Conclusions:

I. Some flowers are plants. (Not follow, ``Some trees are plants'' does
not ensure any of those trees are flowers.)\\
II. All flowers are plants. (Not follow, no statement links all flowers
to plants; all flowers are trees trees but trees → plants is only
``some''.)\\
So, Neither I nor II follows.

Thus, correct option is (a).

