Q.87 \textbf{In the following question, a pair of words is given in
capital letters, followed by five answer options consisting of word
pairs. Choose the option in which the relationship between the two
words} \textbf{most closely matches the relationship between the given
pair.}

\textbf{PROFLIGATE : FRUGALITY}\\
\textbf{1. Mendacious: Truth}\\
\textbf{2. Ubiquitous : Presence}\\
\textbf{3. Punctilious: Detail}\\
\textbf{4. Gregarious : Sociable}\\
\textbf{5. Insipid : Bland}

A. Uniquitous : Presence\\
B. Insipid : Bland\\
C. Punctilious : Detail\\
D. Mendacious : Truth

Answer: D

Sol: Given:\\
PROFLIGATE : FRUGALITY\\
Logic:\\
Relationship is antonymy---profligate (extravagant, wasteful) is the
opposite trait of frugality (economy/thrift). It's an adjective set
against the noun naming the opposite quality.

Explanation:\\
A. Ubiquitous : Presence --- not opposite; presence is related but not
an antonym (and the noun form matching would be ubiquity).

B. Insipid : Bland --- synonyms, not opposites.

C. Punctilious : Detail --- describes attentiveness to detail; not an
opposite pair.

D. Mendacious : Truth --- antonyms (lying vs truth); mirrors adjective
vs opposite noun.

Hence option d is the correct answer.
\end{quote}

