Q.90 \textbf{In a 20 L mixture the ratio of juice to water is 3:2. How
much juice is in the mixture?}

A. 10 L\\
B. 8 L\\
C. 12 L\\
D. 14 L

Answer: C

Sol: Given:\\
Total Mixture = 20 L\\
Ratio of Juice and Water = 3: 2\\
To find:\\
Quantity of Juice in mixture\\
Solution:\\
Let the Quantity of Juice = 3x\\
and the quantity of water = 2x\\
Now,\\
3\emph{x} + 2\emph{x} = 20\\
5\emph{x} = 20\\
\emph{x} = 4\hspace{0pt}\\
Quantity of Juice = 3\emph{x} = 3 × 4 = 12\emph{L}\\
Hence, option C is the correct answer.\hspace{0pt}

