Diamonds = 2 × Spades; Hearts = Diamonds.

Logic:\\
Let Spades = S =\textgreater{} Diamonds = 2S and Hearts = 2S.

Red: H + D = 2S + 2S = 4S = 8 =\textgreater{} S = 2.

Then Diamonds = 4, Hearts = 4.

Black: Spades + Clubs = 7 =\textgreater{} 2 + Clubs = 7 =\textgreater{}
Clubs = 5.

He has 4 Hearts, 4 Diamonds, 2 Spades, so Clubs must be 5 to make 7
black cards.\\
Hence, option A is the correct answer.

Q.95 \textbf{Input: 85 kite 23 lamp 62 brush}\\
\textbf{Step 1: brush 85 kite 23 lamp 62}\\
\textbf{Step 2: brush 85 kite 62 23 lamp}\\
\textbf{Step 3: brush 85 kite 62 lamp 23}\\
\textbf{Which of the following describes the logic best?}

A. Placing smallest word first; largest number second\\
B. Placing words alphabetically from left and numbers in descending
order\\
C. Words on odd positions and numbers on even positions\\
D. Alphabetically placing words from start; numbers in increasing order
from end

Answer: B

Sol: Given -\\
Input: 85 kite 23 lamp 62 brush\\
Step I: brush 85 kite 23 lamp 62 --- (place the alphabetically first
word brush at the start)\\
Step II: brush 85 kite 62 23 lamp --- (place the next largest number 62
so numbers go in descending order)\\
Step III: brush 85 kite 62 lamp 23 --- (place the next word lamp so
words go in alphabetical order)\\
Logic = Numbers are arranged in decreasing order and words are arranged
in alphabetical order, in an alternating sequence (word, number, word,
number, \ldots). According to options, option (B) will follow: Placing
words alphabetically from left and numbers in descending order.

Q.96 \textbf{Input: blue 42 rose 71 violet 13 orange}\\
\textbf{Which of the following would be Step 3 if the logic is:}\\
\textbf{Step 1: Alphabetical arrangement of words from left}\\
\textbf{Step 2: Numbers arranged in descending order from the end?}

A. Blue orange rose violet 42 71 13\\
B. Blue orange rose violet 71 42 13\\
C. Blue orange rose violet 71 13 42\\
D. Orange violet rose blue 71 42 13

Answer: B

Sol: Given - Input: blue 42 rose 71 violet 13 orange\\
Step 1: Alphabetical arrangement of words from left\\
Step 2: Numbers arranged in descending order from the end\\
Logic = words are placed from the left in alphabetical order, and
numbers are placed from the right in descending order, in alternate
steps.\hspace{0pt}Step I: blue orange rose violet 42 71 13 - (Arrange
words in alphabetical order from the left)\\
Step II: blue orange rose violet 71 42 13 - (Arrange numbers in
descending order from the right end)\\
Step III: blue orange rose violet 71 42 13 - (No further moves needed;
arrangement complete)\\
According to options, option (b) will follow.
\end{quote}

