Option C is the correct answer.

Q.100 \textbf{Input: dance, apple, zebra, kite, fan, bottle}\\
\textbf{Step I: apple, dance, zebra, kite, fan, bottle}\\
\textbf{Step II: apple, bottle, dance, zebra, kite, fan}\\
\textbf{Step III: apple, bottle, dance, fan, zebra, kite}\\
\textbf{Step IV: apple, bottle, dance, fan, kite, zebra}\\
\textbf{Question: What is the logic followed in the above arrangement?}

A. Descending alphabetical order left to right\\
B. Alphabetical arrangement from right to left\\
C. Largest word to left, smallest word to right in alternating steps\\
D. Ascending alphabetical order with one word rearranged in each step

Answer: D

Sol: Given -- Input: dance, apple, zebra, kite, fan, bottle\\
Step I: apple, dance, zebra, kite, fan, bottle -- (place the
alphabetically smallest word at the left)\\
Step II: apple, bottle, dance, zebra, kite, fan\\
Step III: apple, bottle, dance, fan, zebra, kite\\
Step IV: apple, bottle, dance, fan, kite, zebra\\
Logic = Arrange the list in ascending (A→Z) alphabetical order, fixing
one word in its correct position per step (left to right).\\
According to options, option (D) will follow.

Hence option D is the correct answer.
\end{quote}

