Nonetheless, constructing and retaining such infrastructure requires
capital and long-term vision. Equity issues are also important: lines
need to serve low-income communities along with commercial hubs so that
all citizens have a benefit. Finally, when properly planned, public
transportation promotes economic efficiency, social mobility, and a
cleaner city.}

A. Public transport is outdated in modern cities\\
B. Investment in roads for private vehicles is more practical
\end{quote}

