himself of a fully realized recognition. Meanwhile, the slave, through
labour and self-transformation, attains a deeper awareness of autonomy,
demonstrating that freedom is not given but achieved through negation
and \_\_\_\_\_\_ (4). Spirit (Geist) emerges as the reconciliation of
these conflicts-not a static substance but a dynamic process of
self-realization. Spirit unfolds historically, manifesting itself (5) in
institutions, culture, and philosophy, gradually moving toward absolute
knowing. This historical progression is not linear but dialectical,
driven by the negation of old forms and the emergence of new ones.}

A. Transforms\\
B. Interrupts\\
C. Interrupt\\
D. Disabuses

Answer: A

Sol: The word that can be filled in the blank is `Transforms' to make
the sentence grammatically and contextually correct.

• `Transforms' (3rd-person singular present of ``transform'') means
``changes in form, nature, or character.'' It parallels ``shapes'':
``consciousness \textbf{shapes and transforms} its own reality.''• As
per the context, the word `transforms' fits in very well \& hence, it is
the correct option.

\textbf{Meanings of other given words and why they are incorrect:}\\
• \textbf{Interrupts} -- means ``breaks the continuity of'';
semantically mismatched with the constructive process described; also
the (b) and (c) options duplicate the same verb.

• \textbf{Interrupts} -- duplicate of (b) with the same issue.

• \textbf{Disabuses} -- means ``persuades someone that a belief is
mistaken''; typically takes a human object (``disabuses someone''), so
``consciousness \ldots{} disabuses its own reality'' is ill-formed in
context.

• Thus, all the other given words have different meanings and do not fit
the constructive, parallel structure with ``shapes.''
\end{quote}

