\textbf{The truth of the self-conscious individual lies not in its
immediate certainty, but in the dialectical movement of its becoming.
Consciousness, in its pursuit of knowledge, initially assumes that its
object is something external and independent. Yet, through the labour of
experience, it discovers that this object is not truly separate but
\_\_\_\_\_\_(1) by consciousness itself.}

\textbf{The apparent duality of subject and object is thus sublated in
