preserving records/documents}.

Q.149 \textbf{Which sentence contains a word that is spelled
incorrectly?}

A. The scientist explained the hypothesis behind the experiment clearly.

B. The new hybrid model of the car is both fuel-efficient and stylish.\\
C. The therapist used hypnosis to help the patient recall past
memories.\\
D. It's important to maintain hygenc practices to prevent illness.

Answer: D

Sol: \textbf{Option (d)} is the \textbf{incorrectly} spelt sentence.

\textbf{Correct spelling is:} `` \textbf{hygienic} practices'' ---
\emph{hygienic} means clean and sanitary; it relates to maintaining
health by preventing disease through cleanliness. \emph{(Hindi:}
स्वच्छतापूर्ण\emph{,} स्वास्थ्यकर\emph{)} \textbf{Example:} Doctors emphasize
\textbf{hygienic} practices like regular handwashing.

\textbf{Meanings of all the given options:}\\
· \textbf{(a)}\emph{hypothesis} --- a proposed explanation made on the
basis of limited evidence. \emph{(Hindi:} परिकल्पना\emph{)}\\
· \textbf{(b)}\emph{hybrid} --- something made by combining two
different elements; in cars, a vehicle using two power sources.
\emph{(Hindi:} संकर\emph{)}\\
· \textbf{(c)}\emph{hypnosis} --- a trance-like state of focused
attention and increased suggestibility. \emph{(Hindi:} सम्मोहन\emph{)}\\
· \textbf{(d)}\emph{hygienic} (correct form) --- conducive to
maintaining health and preventing disease; clean. \emph{(Hindi:}
स्वच्छतापूर्ण\emph{/}स्वास्थ्यकर\emph{)}

Q.150 \textbf{Identify the word in this sentence that contains an
error.}\\
\textbf{The keys are inside the table drawer.}

A. keys\\
B. drawer\\
C. table\\
D. inside

Answer: D

Sol: Option (d) contains an error.

\textbf{Detailed explanation of error:} While \textbf{inside} is not
inherently wrong, the \textbf{idiomatic} and preferred preposition for
routine location with containers like drawers is \textbf{in}: ``The keys
are \textbf{in} the table drawer.'' We typically reserve \textbf{inside}
for emphatic contrast of interior vs exterior ( \emph{inside vs
outside}) or when entering a space, whereas neutral location takes
\textbf{in}.

\textbf{Grammatical rule used:} Use \textbf{in} for general location
within bounded areas/containers (in a box, in a room, in a drawer). Use
\textbf{inside} when you need contrast or emphasis on the interior (
\emph{Stay inside the house}).

\textbf{Example:}\emph{Your passport is \textbf{in}the top drawer.} /
\emph{It's raining; please stay \textbf{inside}the house.}

\textbf{Information booster:} In formal written English, avoid ``
\textbf{inside of}'' for simple location. Prefer \textbf{in} ( \emph{in
the drawer}). \textbf{Within} can be used in formal contexts of limits (
\emph{within the box/limits}), but not typically for everyday placement
like keys in a drawer.

Q.151 \textbf{Find the incorrect part of the sentence:}\\
\textbf{One must keep his promises.}

A. One\\
B. No error\\
C. must keep\\
D. his promises

Answer: D

Sol: Option \textbf{(d)} contains an error.

\textbf{Detailed explanation:} The indefinite pronoun \textbf{``one''}
must be followed by the \textbf{possessive ``one's,''} not ``his/her.''
Therefore, the correct sentence is: \textbf{``One must keep one's
promises.''} The pronoun-antecedent agreement requires consistency in
person; mixing \textbf{one \ldots{} his} is considered a mismatch in
formal English.

\textbf{Grammatical rule used:} Maintain \textbf{person and number
consistency} with indefinite pronouns: \emph{one → one's}, \emph{someone
→ their} (in modern usage), etc.

\textbf{Example:}\emph{One should mind \textbf{one's}manners in public.}

\textbf{Info booster / exceptions:} In contemporary English,
\textbf{singular they} is widely used for gender neutrality (
\emph{``Everyone should keep \textbf{their}promises''}), but when the
sentence starts with \textbf{one}, the traditional, most formal pairing
is \textbf{one's}.

Q.152 \textbf{Select the most appropriate option to fill in the
